\title{Typed bindings: a bound variable carries its declared type}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{27a6c07}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The fix of the findings E1-F1 to E1-F6 in the machine. A binding made for a \code{\verb~|let~}, for the argument of a beta redex and for a comparison variable now carries the binder's declared type; the expected-type rule applies only when the domains are identical; and the expected codomain is no longer stored as the lambda's own. A sixth shape found by a systematic search, the K rule on a major premise that is the application of a let variable, is closed by a decline rule; 78 new hostile exports came with the fix.}

\p{Gates: per declaration against the reference engine with the default set, 0 soundness and 0 completeness differences on the tutorial and bugs tests, the Cedar slice, reachability, Init, Std, 16 Mathlib slices and the 230 tests; the hostile matrix of 32 switch sets times 407 rows, 13,024 judgments, with nothing flagged; the mutants for the generic tier and the default set; and through the launcher the 78 rows under two switch sets, 156 runs with no difference from the official verdicts. The fix costs no measurable wall clock. In ticks the default set grows by 2.63 \% on the Cedar slice and by about 0.3 \% on Init and Std, all of it from the restriction of the expected-type rule. A further finding, E1-F7 with two variants, was open at the end of the day; its rows are in the suite.}

\p{Detail: \src{docs/design/review/official-divergence.md}, \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M5.md}. Commit \commit{27a6c07}. Session: [exactness](ses-874D). Related: [typed bindings stay in the default](dec-0DSI), [a let whose declared type differs from the type of its value](ex-GZ3D), [why an evaluator that types values cannot match the kernel](ins-AAXM).}
